{
  "technical_and_design_decisions": [
    "Target Java 17 with Spring Boot 3.x / Spring Cloud Stream 4.x, consistent with the Spring Framework 6.0 baseline stated in the specification.",
    "Each module is delivered as a standalone, auto-configured Spring Boot application following the Spring Cloud Stream app-starter conventions: sink apps bind to Sink, source apps bind to Source, processor apps bind to Processor.",
    "Port the existing XD module logic (message handlers, channel adapters, option classes) rather than redesigning: convert XD XML module configuration into Java-based Spring Integration configuration classes.",
    "Expose module options as typed @ConfigurationProperties classes with configuration metadata, replacing XD module option annotations.",
    "Auto-configuration guarded by @ConditionalOnProperty/@ConditionalOnClass so the apps can be composed and customized via properties.",
    "Testing strategy uses embedded or in-process test doubles instead of external infrastructure: embedded MQTT broker (Mosquitto) for mqtt, mock Splunk HTTP endpoint for splunk, embedded H2 database for jdbc, a loopback TCP echo server for tcp, MockRestServiceServer-style mock HTTP server for http-client, and real but simple shell commands for shell.",
    "Aggregator processor uses a configurable message store with an in-memory default and a JDBC store for persistence tests; correlation, release, and aggregation SpEL expressions are externalized as properties.",
    "App packaging (generated binder-specific runnable jars) reuses the existing s-c-s repo Maven plugin/conventions; no new packaging tooling is built.",
    "Maven is used as the build system with a multi-module structure mirroring the existing s-c-s app-starters repository layout."
  ],
  "assumptions": [
    "The original Spring XD module source code for all eight modules is available, working, and serves as the functional baseline; no new features beyond the port are in scope.",
    "A single developer performs all work and is experienced with Spring Integration, Spring Cloud Stream, and the XD codebase.",
    "Wire-level behavior and message formats remain unchanged from the XD modules; no backward-compatibility shims beyond the port are required.",
    "Access to live external services (production MQTT broker, Splunk instance) is not required; embedded/mocked equivalents are sufficient for acceptance.",
    "Effort covers design, coding, unit tests, integration tests, README documentation, and incorporation of code review feedback; it excludes project management, release publishing to public repositories, marketing materials, and long-term maintenance.",
    "The s-c-s repository already has parent POMs, CI pipeline templates, and checkstyle/license conventions that only need minor extension for the new modules.",
    "User stories U1-U8 are independent; shared infrastructure work is performed once and reused by all modules.",
    "Defect density is typical for a code port of this kind; the estimates include a normal allowance for debugging and test fixes."
  ],
  "activities": [
    {
      "activity_id": "A1",
      "activity_name": "Requirements analysis and XD codebase assessment",
      "activity_description": "Review the eight XD modules (mqtt, null, shell, splunk, tcp, jdbc, aggregator, http-client), inventory their options, message handlers, XML configuration, and dependencies, and confirm the sink/source/processor role for each in the s-c-s model.",
      "most_likely_effort": 8
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A2",
      "activity_name": "Repository, build, and module skeleton setup",
      "activity_description": "Create the multi-module Maven structure for the eight app starters, wire parent POMs, dependency management, checkstyle/license rules, and CI job definitions, and generate empty Spring Boot application skeletons with Sink/Source/Processor bindings.",
      "most_likely_effort": 16
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A3",
      "activity_name": "Shared porting conventions and test infrastructure",
      "activity_description": "Implement shared base classes and utilities used by all ports: properties-to-adapter mapping patterns, common integration-test base classes, SpEL evaluation helpers, and the app-starter documentation snippet template.",
      "most_likely_effort": 12
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A4",
      "activity_name": "Port null sink module (U2)",
      "activity_description": "Port the trivial message-discarding sink: auto-configuration, binding to Sink, unit/integration test verifying messages are consumed, POM, and README.",
      "most_likely_effort": 8
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A5",
      "activity_name": "Port shell sink module (U3)",
      "activity_description": "Port the shell-command message handler and its options (command, arguments, working directory, timeout, charset) to a @ConfigurationProperties class and Java config; write unit tests and integration tests executing real shell commands; add POM and README.",
      "most_likely_effort": 12
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A6",
      "activity_name": "Port tcp sink module (U5)",
      "activity_description": "Port the TCP outbound adapter configuration: connection factory options (host, port, SSL, serializer/deserializer, timeouts, close semantics) as properties, Java-based SI configuration, unit tests, and integration tests against a loopback echo server; add POM and README.",
      "most_likely_effort": 20
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A7",
      "activity_name": "Port mqtt sink module (U1)",
      "activity_description": "Port the Paho-based MQTT outbound message handler: broker URL, client id, topic (including SpEL), QoS, retained flag, and credentials as properties; Java config; unit tests plus integration tests against an embedded Mosquitto broker; add POM and README.",
      "most_likely_effort": 24
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A8",
      "activity_name": "Port splunk sink module (U4)",
      "activity_description": "Port the Splunk SDK-based message handler: host, port, scheme, credentials, index, and source/sourcetype options as properties; Java config; unit tests and integration tests against a mocked Splunk HEC endpoint; add POM and README.",
      "most_likely_effort": 24
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A9",
      "activity_name": "Port jdbc source module (U6)",
      "activity_description": "Port the JDBC polling inbound adapter: query, update query, max rows, split, column mapping, and metadata-store options as properties; Java config with poller configuration; unit tests and integration tests against an embedded H2 database verifying polling and state tracking; add POM and README.",
      "most_likely_effort": 32
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A10",
      "activity_name": "Port aggregator processor module (U7)",
      "activity_description": "Port the stateful aggregator: correlation and release strategies, aggregation SpEL, message-store abstraction (in-memory default, JDBC store for tests), timeout and group-expiry handling as properties; Java config bound to Processor; extensive unit tests and integration tests covering windowing, release, and restart recovery; add POM and README.",
      "most_likely_effort": 48
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A11",
      "activity_name": "Port http-client processor module (U8)",
      "activity_description": "Port the HTTP outbound gateway processor: URL/method/headers/body expressions, expected response type, reply expression, and charset options as properties; Java config bound to Processor; unit tests and integration tests against a mock HTTP server; add POM and README.",
      "most_likely_effort": 24
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A12",
      "activity_name": "End-to-end stream integration verification",
      "activity_description": "Assemble and run representative pipelines (jdbc source -> aggregator processor -> splunk sink; mqtt/http-client/tcp/shell/null combinations) using a test binder to verify the modules interoperate correctly as a streaming pipeline.",
      "most_likely_effort": 16
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A13",
      "activity_name": "Aggregate documentation and release preparation",
      "activity_description": "Produce the consolidated reference documentation for all eight app starters, verify property metadata tables, prepare version/changelog entries, and finalize artifacts for release readiness (without performing the actual publish).",
      "most_likely_effort": 8
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A14",
      "activity_name": "Code review, refactoring, and final hardening",
      "activity_description": "Address code review feedback across all modules, normalize naming and configuration conventions, remove dead code, fix residual test flakiness, and perform a final full build and test pass.",
      "most_likely_effort": 16
    }
  ],
  "reported_total": {
    "most_likely_effort": 268
  }
}
